WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.550
Anyone who has seen the Star Wars films and
dug into the franchise's vast canon knows

00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:06.580
that lightsabers come in a variety of colors.

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:11.680
For the most part, Jedi wield sabers that
are blue or green colors that represent the

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:13.920
two biggest schools of thought within the
Jedi Order.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:18.220
Green is most commonly chosen by the Consulars,
who focus on their mental knowledge of the

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:18.760
Force.

00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:23.040
Blue is most often seen in the hands of Jedi
Guardians, who focus on learning combat and

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:24.040
becoming warriors.

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:29.280
Those who have aligned themselves with the
dark side, mostly Sith Lords, flash red lightsabers

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:29.820
in combat.

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:31.500
And as for purple lightsabers?

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:36.070
Mace Windu's violet-colored blade was only
introduced to the franchise because actor

00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:41.780
Samuel L. Jackson put in a personal request
to Star Wars creator George Lucas for a lightsaber

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:46.960
bearing his favorite color… and Samuel L.
Jackson gets what Samuel L. Jackson wants.

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:51.400
In the expanded Star Wars universe, however,
there are plenty more colors of lightsabers

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:52.040
to go around.

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:55.260
Although extremely rare, yellow lightsabers
are among them.

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:59.880
Just like the blue and green lightsabers,
the yellow lightsaber is associated with an

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:03.500
important school of thought within the Jedi
Order: that of the Sentinels.

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:08.560
Star Wars lore explains that the Sentinels
seek a balance between the Consulars and the

00:01:08.980 --> 00:01:13.580
Guardians, and also wish to educate themselves
on other more practical aspects of life such

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:14.820
as tracking techniques and espionage.

00:01:15.770 --> 00:01:20.780
Unlike some others in the Jedi Order, Sentinels
recognize that the Force isn't actually the

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:21.460
solution to everything.

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:29.500
"Mmm, A Jedi uses the Force for knowledge
and defense — never for attack."

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:35.000
The yellow lightsaber is most commonly seen
in the Jedi Temple Guards' pikes on the Star

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:36.920
Wars animated series The Clone Wars.

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:43.100
The Temple Guards wield double-bladed yellow
sabers, much like the dual-ended red weapon

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:45.540
Darth Maul hefted around before it was sliced
in half.

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:49.969
These lightsabers don't personally belong
to the Temple Guards, but are instead the

00:01:49.969 --> 00:01:51.680
property of the position they hold.

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:56.600
Additionally, there are other rare sightings
of yellow lightsabers including in the hands

00:01:56.600 --> 00:02:01.460
of bounty hunter Asajj Ventress, who apparently
found her lightsaber on the black market.

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:07.320
Ventress' blade was identical to those of
the Jedi, rather than the more blade-like

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:09.480
appearance of the pikes wielded by the Temple
Guard.

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:14.400
Another Star Wars character said to have carried
a yellow lightsaber is Anakin Skywalker's

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.260
Padawan learner Ahsoka Tano.

00:02:16.709 --> 00:02:22.200
Though George Lucas nixed the idea of Ahsoka
using a full-on yellow saber on Star Wars:

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:27.080
The Clone Wars, Ahsoka's mostly green saber
was altered to give off a slightly yellow

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:27.600
glow.

00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:32.100
In essence, a lightsaber's color reveals something
about its wielder and their personality.

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:37.380
Lucasfilm's Pablo Hidalgo has explained that
the Kyber crystals used to make lightsabers

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:38.800
start out colorless.

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:44.180
The crystals only take on a color once they
has been gathered by a Jedi Padawan, and a

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:48.220
bond between the crystal and the Jedi has
been formed during the creation of the lightsaber.

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:53.850
There's even been an instance in which a yellow
saber was made from unstable red saber crystal,

00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:58.960
when Jedi Jaden Korr purified it and the crystal
turned yellow, granting him his third lightsaber.

00:02:59.650 --> 00:03:04.120
It's been suggested that perhaps the reason
so few yellow sabers are seen in the era of

00:03:04.129 --> 00:03:09.569
the Clone Wars is because so few Sentinels
still exist in the Jedi Order, with most Jedi

00:03:09.569 --> 00:03:12.120
either falling into the category of Consular
or Guardian.

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:16.760
Another theory is that because the Sentinels
focus so much of their energy on learning

00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:21.060
skills outside of the Force, they may still
exist but they remain so low on the radar

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:23.800
that they rarely have to whip out their yellow
lightsabers.

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:28.879
Because of their real-world skills, their
missions outside of the Jedi Temple didn't

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:30.040
require them to use combat.

00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:34.400
Instead, they'd resort to their real-world
knowledge that wouldn't have required them

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:35.680
to show off their lightsaber skills.

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:41.439
The Star Wars universe is ever-expanding,
with new movies and TV shows coming even after

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:43.340
the Skywalker saga concludes.

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:48.440
Lucasfilm is currently preparing to launch
an Obi-Wan Kenobi series on the Disney+ streaming

00:03:48.440 --> 00:03:53.000
platform to follow the first live-action Star
Wars show, The Mandalorian.

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:58.460
With any luck, fans may see yellow lightsabers
in all their glory all over the place in the

00:03:58.460 --> 00:03:58.980
years to come.

